ype":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"to use its backend types. Any SwiftLog ","type":"text"},{"code":"LogHandler","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" can be supplied by the factory.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Each call replaces both settings. Omitting the factory restores YubiKit’s backend;"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"omitting the level uses the selected handler’s level. Changes apply to existing sessions,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"though logs already in progress may use the previous settings.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"YubiKit’s configuration does not affect other libraries. To share your app’s backend,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"pass its factory explicitly; global ","type":"text"},{"code":"LoggingSystem.bootstrap","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" does not select YubiKit’s backend.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"Factories may run concurrently and must not log through YubiKit themselves.","type":"text"}]},{"text":"Traffic logging","level":3,"type":"heading","anchor":"Traffic-logging"},{"code":["Logging.configure(logLevel: .trace)"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Raw traffic and SCP plaintext logs require "},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"YubiKit to be compiled with "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"DEBUG"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":".","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"Neither configuration nor a custom backend can enable them in other builds.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"Custom connections are responsible for their own traffic logging.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"style":"warning","content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Debug logs can include account names and credential identifiers."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Trace logs can include PINs, credentials, and cryptographic keys. Protect or redact logs before sharing them."}],"type":"paragraph"}],"name":"Warning","type":"aside"},{"anchor":"Custom-backends","level":3,"text":"Custom backends","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Labels identify categories, such as ","type":"text"},{"code":"com.yubico.YubiKit.OATH","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" or ","type":"text"},{"code":"com.yubico.YubiKit.FIDO","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":".","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"Metadata carries details such as byte counts and error codes; the default backend displays"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"these as "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"key=value"},{"type":"text","text":" pairs. Message wording and metadata keys are not a stable API."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Your backend controls formatting, storage, and export. YubiKit does not retain log messages."}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"seeAlsoSections":[{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/yubikit-swift.YubiKit\/documentation\/YubiKit\/GettingStarted","doc:\/\/yubikit-swift.YubiKit\/documentation\/YubiKit\/Logging"],"title":"Preparing your project","anchor":"Preparing-your-project","generated":true}],"references":{"doc://yubikit-swift.YubiKit/documentation/YubiKit":{"role":"collection","identifier":"doc:\/\/yubikit-swift.YubiKit\/documentation\/YubiKit","abstract":[{"text":"Connect and run commands on the different applications on a YubiKey. The framework support connecting using NFC, Lightning and USB.","type":"text"}],"url":"\/documentation\/yubikit","type":"topic","images":[{"identifier":"documentation-header.png","type":"icon"}],"title":"YubiKit","kind":"symbol"},"doc://yubikit-swift.YubiKit/documentation/YubiKit/Logging/configure(logLevel:factory:)":{"abstract":[{"text":"Sets YubiKit’s log level and backend.","type":"text"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/yubikit-swift.YubiKit\/documentation\/YubiKit\/Logging\/configure(logLevel:factory:)","url":"\/documentation\/yubi